expr main (please advise)

let message "`Please advise` is stiff. Say what you need."
let description "Suggests warmer, clearer wording than `please advise` in emails."
let kind "Style"
let becomes ["please let me know what you think", "please let me know"]

# True positives
test "We think please advise the plan is solid." "We think please let me know what you think the plan is solid."
test "Yesterday please advise the draft was sent." "Yesterday please let me know what you think the draft was sent."
test "We think please advise the plan is solid." "We think please let me know what you think the plan is solid."
test "Yesterday please advise the draft was sent." "Yesterday please let me know what you think the draft was sent."
test "We think please advise the plan is solid." "We think please let me know what you think the plan is solid."
test "Yesterday please advise the draft was sent." "Yesterday please let me know what you think the draft was sent."
test "We think please advise the plan is solid." "We think please let me know what you think the plan is solid."
test "Yesterday please advise the draft was sent." "Yesterday please let me know what you think the draft was sent."
test "We think please advise the plan is solid." "We think please let me know what you think the plan is solid."
test "Please advise the plan." "Please let me know what you think the plan."

# True negatives
allows "She will advise the board."
allows "Please let me know."
allows "He wants to advise them."
allows "We advise caution."
allows "Her advice was kind."
allows "The report is ready."
allows "Send the file tomorrow."
